# Upstream baseline for the mainline H5000M build.
#
# WHY openwrt/openwrt main (SNAPSHOT) AND NOT 25.12
# -------------------------------------------------
# Hiveton H5000M support was added upstream by
#   6487cc9a1f  "mediatek: add support for Hiveton H5000M"   (2026-01-09)
# and that commit is only on `main`.  Verified against the published images:
#
#   releases/25.12.0 .. 25.12.5 -> profiles.json contains NO hiveton_h5000m
#   snapshots/                  -> profiles.json contains hiveton_h5000m
#
# The openwrt-25.12 *branch* head does carry the device (cherry-picked after
# the 25.12.5 tag), but no released 25.12.x image does, so SNAPSHOT `main` is
# simultaneously the newest and the only mainline upstream that ships H5000M
# firmware today.  It is also what every in-tree plugin for this board is
# verified against (luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol: "OpenWrt SNAPSHOT";
# ddimension feed: `stable/snapshot/aarch64_cortex-a53`).
#
# Set OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=openwrt-25.12 to build the 25.12 branch instead once
# 25.12.6 ships the device.
OPENWRT_REPO_URL=https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt.git
OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=main

# Reproducible baseline.  Two different facts live in this block and they are
# NOT the same fact:
#
#   * the revision the PATCH STACK is aligned to — the one
#     scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh verifies every patch against;
#   * the last revision a FULL BUILD (image + apk repository + all three publish
#     gates) was observed to pass on.
#
# They coincided at 0f8cceb, then stopped coinciding when mainline bumped
# nftables 1.1.6 -> 1.1.7 and libnftnl 1.3.1 -> 1.3.2 between 0f8cceb and 99426e4
# (both fullcone userspace patches had to be regenerated — see
# install_nftables_patches), and they coincide again at 058da17 below.
#
# 2026-11-17 upstream-sync review: 99426e4 -> 058da17
# ---------------------------------------------------
# 058da17 is the revision the 2026-11-16 scheduled build actually built and
# passed with every gate (image + apk repository + attestation + publish +
# Pages), so it satisfies both halves at once.  What the 1074 upstream commits
# between 99426e4 and that build did, and did not, touch:
#
#   * nftables 1.1.7-r1 and libnftnl 1.3.2-r1 — UNCHANGED, so
#     nftables-patches/100-fullcone-expression.patch and
#     libnftnl-patches/100-fullnftl-expression.patch apply byte-for-byte as
#     before.  Nothing to regenerate.
#   * firewall4 — its source commit moved b6e5157 -> 3722ead ("firewall4: update
#     to Git HEAD (2026-11-08)", which is `main`'s 3722ead as of this review).
#     firewall4-patches/100-fullcone-support.patch touches
#     templates/ruleset.uc, templates/zone-masq.uc and ucode/fw4.uc, so it had to
#     be re-checked: `git apply --check` against 3722ead passes, and the 11-16
#     build is the proof that it also applies inside the real build.
#   * kernel — still 6.18.60 (LINUX_VERSION-6.18 = .60); the 11-16 build reported
#     kernel_abi=ac7024928df204cd6201adcbc2974cb5 for it.
#
# 2026-11-23 upstream-sync review: 058da17 -> 14a07b7 (108 commits, NOT yet
# promoted to the pin — see the last paragraph of this block)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the 108 commits do and do not touch:
#
#   * nftables (1.1.7), libnftnl (1.3.2) and firewall4 (source 3722ead) — all
#     UNCHANGED.  scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh --ref 14a07b7 passes
#     all four userspace layers (nftables, libnftnl, firewall4, mt76) plus both
#     tree patches and every Nikki-RS anchor and clash-rs hash pin.
#   * kernel 6.18.60 -> 6.18.64 (f7d14dc28 -> a5383abb3 -> 75fde714f).  The
#     kernel ABI moves with it, which is exactly why the kmods and the pinned
#     sing-box live in the image / this project's repository and not upstream.
#   * toolchain: gcc 15 becomes the default (fd3b9d467).  This is the one change
#     in the range that can break a package build for reasons unrelated to our
#     patches, so it needs a real build, not a patch dry-run.  Half of it was
#     cleared on 2026-11-23 by compiling the two pieces that can be built in
#     isolation under gcc 15.3.0: the patched libnftnl 1.3.2 + nftables 1.1.7
#     (inside `verify-upstream-integration.sh --compile`) and the out-of-tree
#     local-packages/nft-fullcone module against 6.18.64 headers, which still
#     carries `-Werror -Wall` and compiles clean.  The image itself is the part
#     that remains unproven.
#   * netfilter.mk: added kmod-nf-xtables and *_LEGACY symbols, and rewired
#     kmod-ipt-*/kmod-nft-compat to depend on it.  Additive; the kmod list here
#     gets the new dependency through kconfig automatically.
#   * mediatek target: only mt7981/mt7986 DTS and base-files changed.  The
#     hiveton_h5000m DTS and the two patches/ hunks are untouched.
#
# Deliberately a fixed revision, not "whatever main's head is": `latest` is the
# mode that follows the branch head; this is the reproducible one.  Bumping it is
# therefore a review action with evidence attached (a build that passed), not a
# scheduled edit.
#
# Why a pin cannot just chase main every day: a patch regenerated against
# nftables 1.1.7 cannot be applied to 1.1.6 — 1.1.7 added `<*>` start-condition
# prefixes to the NAT keyword rules in src/scanner.l — so a pin whose value
# tracks a moving target is not a pin.
#
# The patch-stack half is machine-verified by
# scripts/verify-upstream-integration.sh (also a PR gate); the full-build half is
# recorded as a separate sentence here rather than being allowed to blur into it.
#
# So the pin stays at 058da17 for now: 14a07b7 has the patch-stack evidence above
# but not a full build.  gcc 15 has been cleared for the pieces that can be
# compiled in isolation (patched nftables/libnftnl, and the fullcone module with
# -Werror), so what is actually missing is the assembled image.  The `latest`
# line already builds 14a07b7 today — nothing about the firmware content lags.
# Move the pin to 14a07b78e9ac9d604547533550e6aa41955ac588 (snapshot r0-14a07b7)
# once a scheduled build of that revision has passed image + apk repository +
# publish.  firewall4/mt76 used to be "unverifiable on Windows" (the snapshots
# contain symlinks tar cannot create there); run the verifier in a Linux
# container when you need all four layers judged — the script now prints the exact
# command when it detects that tar failure.
#
# Used when OPENWRT_TRACK=pinned, and recorded as the fallback baseline in
# BUILD-INFO.txt when tracking `latest`.
#
# The kernel ABI moves between snapshots that both call themselves 6.18.x
# (3a22303 -> 8ae0a62b, 0f8cceb -> f3b7e5e1), which is why the kmods and the
# pinned sing-box ship inside the image and in this project's own repository
# rather than being fetched from the official snapshot.
OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION=058da17df29908b0b77099fb522823723c385a5e
OPENWRT_PINNED_SNAPSHOT=r0-058da17

# `latest` (default) follows the branch head on every build — that is the point
# of a scheduled auto-build.  `pinned` builds OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION so a build
# can be reproduced exactly; scripts/local-build.sh --pinned selects it.
OPENWRT_TRACK=latest

# Target triple, as published by OpenWrt.
OPENWRT_TARGET=mediatek
OPENWRT_SUBTARGET=filogic
OPENWRT_PROFILE=hiveton_h5000m
OPENWRT_ARCH=aarch64_cortex-a53
OPENWRT_IMAGE_PREFIX=openwrt-mediatek-filogic-hiveton_h5000m

# Optional fallback modem stack.  luci-app-mt5700m (the FAN789 panel for the
# built-in MT5700M) hard-depends on `ubus-at-daemon` and `sms-tool_q`, and both
# are packaged only by the QModem feed.  write_feeds_conf() therefore appends
# this feed *only* when ENABLE_MT5700M=true; a wwand build never sees it, since
# the two stacks are mutually exclusive and QModem brings its own drivers.
QMODEM_REPO_URL=https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git
QMODEM_REPO_BRANCH=main
